From a19b1279d75dd1306c6eac291e985657f988780c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: P Praneesh <ppranees@codeaurora.org>
Date: Thu, 7 Jan 2021 16:32:30 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: dp_tx perf improvements

 Contains below changes,
	1. Add branch prediction in tx path
	2. Allow fast tx completion by freeing skb when stats is disabled.
	3. Remove mod operator overhead for dst ring access to avoid(to be profiled)
	4. Lockless tcl ring usage since rings are selected per cpu

Sample stats disable command:
echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/ath11k/qcn9000\ hw1.0_0000\:01\:00.0/stats_disable
echo 1 > /sys/kernel/debug/ath11k/ipq8074\ hw2.0/stats_disable

Signed-off-by: Sriram R <srirrama@codeaurora.org>
Signed-off-by: P Praneesh <ppranees@codeaurora.org>
[julius: initialize 'flags' from skb_cb in the tx completion path too -
 it was read uninitialized, so status-requested frames (EAPOL) could
 take the stats-disable fast free and never report their tx status.
 Bound the tx-completion service loop and the soc_dp_stats desc_na dump
 by DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX, like the other loops this patch converts.
 max_tx_ring counts submission rings and this patch raises it to
 DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX + 1 so TCL_CMD can carry tx, but dp->tx_ring[] -
 and with it tx_status, the idr and the per-ring completion srng - is
 only DP_TCL_NUM_RING_MAX wide, and TCL_CMD has no completion ring of
 its own; dp_tx already clamps its own tx_ring[] index for that reason.
 ath11k_core_pre_init() clamps max_tx_ring back only when NSS offload is
 on, so on the host datapath the service loop reached one past
 dp->tx_ring[], read a NULL tx_status and panicked in
 ath11k_dp_tx_completion_handler() as soon as a frame went out on the
 last CPU. desc_na[] is sized the same way, so the stats dump read past
 it and printed a bogus extra ring]
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
